## Explicit: path-A sealed vs residual

### Path-A **sealed** (proved this pass)

| Gate | Evidence |
|------|----------|
| SysCap on exec | `oo_cap_require_sys` before fork |
| No `system(3)` | `fork` + `execvp` argv only (`oo_sys_exec1` is `sh -c` argv form) |
| Child drops classic loader/shell gadgets | Live `/usr/bin/env` child: **no** `LD_PRELOAD`, `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, `DYLD_*`, `BASH_ENV`, `ENV`, `IFS`; `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` forced |
| Child keeps only `OODA_*` / `OO_*` + PATH | Prefix snapshot **before** `clearenv` (avoids post-clearenv getenv false-empty) |
| FFI cap + allow gate | Without `OODA_FFI_ALLOW_DLOPEN=1` → residual Err; non-sys path without ALLOWDIR → Err |
| Absolute path required for allowdir prefix | Relative `libc.so.6` → not under system lib dirs |
| `..` traversal on allowdir | realpath canonical compare + trailing `/` boundary (not prefix-`/tmp/foo` vs `/tmp/foobar`) |
| Nested `oo_dlopen` (constructor re-entry) | `g_ffi_dlopen_depth` refuse **before** non-recursive `g_ffi_dlopen_mu` (no self-deadlock) |
| Concurrent dlopen serialize | process-wide `g_ffi_dlopen_mu` around allow→verify→dlopen→register |
| Handle table under mutex | register / lookup / take-for-close |
| Write fail-closed without WRITEDIR | unset `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` → deny all writes |
| Write `..` / relative / outside realpath | denied (`path not under OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`) |
| Write leaf symlink escape (existing symlink to outside) | realpath leaves writedir → deny |
| Write leaf symlink race (swap after allow) | `openat(..., O_NOFOLLOW)` → fail-closed |
| Write create missing leaf | parent realpath under dir + basename not `.`/`..` |
| Minisig required before `dlopen` | unsigned system libc → `missing or invalid minisig` (fail-closed) |
| Minisign child env scrub (**OWN CRITICAL fix**) | `clearenv` + `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` + absolute `/usr/bin`/`/bin` minisign before `execlp` |

### Residual (**not** sealed — honesty)

| Residual | Sev | Why still open |
|----------|-----|----------------|
| Minisig TOCTOU (verify then `dlopen` path string) | **HIGH** | open+close with `O_NOFOLLOW`, then `dlopen(rp_path)` — content replace / rename between verify and load; no `fdlopen` / verify-by-fd |
| Intermediate dir component races | **MED** | leaf `O_NOFOLLOW` only; no `openat` chain / landlock |
| Untrusted-but-signed `.so` constructors | **HIGH** | `RTLD_NOW` runs ctors with full process privileges; nested **`oo_dlopen`** refused, but ctors can raw `dlopen`/`exec`/`write` outside path-A |
| No typed `ffi_call` (good residual) | — | symbol is opaque `sym:%p` only — keeps RCE bar at "load signed code" not "call any ptr" |
| Handle refcount / concurrent dlsym after dlclose | **MED** | documented UAF class; take-under-lock helps double-close only |
| Default pubkey path `/etc/ooda/ffi.pub` missing on host | **MED** | all OS loads fail-closed until ops install trust anchor — feature-dark, not bypass |
| `OO_FFI_PUBKEY_FP_DEFAULT` all-zero + no in-process FP pin | **MED** | prior `-P <hex fp>` was **wrong API** (minisign `-P` = base64 pubkey); removed in OWN fix; FP pin still residual |
| `execlp` fallback after absolute paths | **LOW** | only if abs paths missing; PATH then limited to `/usr/bin:/bin` |
| Parent process still honors its own `LD_PRELOAD` | **INFO** | out of child-env scope; operator/container TCB |
| `OODA_*` policy inheritance into exec children | **MED** | intentional for nested ooda, but widens policy surface (`OODA_FFI_ALLOW_*`, `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`, …) |
| `OO_LD_PRELOAD` / `OODA_LD_PRELOAD` strings kept | **LOW** | ld.so does **not** honor those names; noise only (live proved keep; not a loader bypass) |
| `oo_sys_exec1` / `sh -c` cmdline injection | **INFO** | by-design SysCap power; env gadgets largely sealed |
| Write **hardlink** escape | **HIGH** | live: hardlink of outside file into writedir → `ok=1`, outside content overwritten (`PWNED_HARD`) |
| Write parent-dentry rename race | **MED** | documented; no landlock / `O_PATH` dirfd pin across check+open |
| `read_file` / `path_exists` / `file_size` no WRITEDIR | **MED** | FsCap still any-path read via `fopen` — not T3 write scope but related FS surface |
| CAP_FFI.oot stale on `dlsym`/`dlclose` | **LOW** | doc says residual stubs; code is registered-handle path-A |
| Smokes may lag tip | **MED** | `ffi_dlopen_path_a_smoke` expects `dlopen-ok` on unsigned libc; `caps_matrix` may assume writes without WRITEDIR |

