## Attack matrix

Verdict key:
- **BLOCK** = refused / sealed on live probe or hard fail-closed code path
- **BYPASS** = attack succeeds (escape / gadget)
- **FAIL-CLOSED** = operation denied for everyone (including legit) — secure but may be product-dark
- **FP** = over-refuse legitimate
- **FN** = under-refuse (should block, didn't)

| # | Attack | Expected (path-A) | Actual / code path | FP/FN | Sev |
|---|--------|-------------------|--------------------|-------|-----|
| E1 | Child inherits `LD_PRELOAD` | strip | **BLOCK** — live env child has empty `LD_PRELOAD`; filter drops non-`OODA_`/`OO_` | no FN | — |
| E2 | Child inherits `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` | strip | **BLOCK** — live empty | no FN | — |
| E3 | Child inherits `DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES` | strip | **BLOCK** — live empty | no FN | — |
| E4 | Child inherits `BASH_ENV` / `ENV` | strip | **BLOCK** — live empty | no FN | — |
| E5 | Child inherits attacker `PATH` | force safe PATH | **BLOCK** — `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin` after filter | no FN | — |
| E6 | Child inherits attacker `IFS` | strip | **BLOCK** — live default IFS from shell only if using `sh`; direct `/usr/bin/env` has no IFS | no FN | — |
| E7 | Keep `OODA_*` after clearenv (logic bug) | keep policy keys | **BLOCK bug class** — tip snapshots prefix **before** clearenv (comment documents prior getenv-after-clearenv FN) | fixed in tip DE | — |
| E8 | `OO_LD_PRELOAD` rename bypass | N/A (ld.so) | **no loader FN** — string kept but ld.so ignores; not RCE | n/a | LOW |
| E9 | Policy env leak to untrusted child | document | **residual** — `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`, `OODA_LEAK_TEST` appear in child | residual | MED |
| E10 | `sh -c` via `oo_sys_exec1` shell inject | SysCap-trusted | **by design** with SysCap; env gadgets sealed | n/a | INFO |
| D1 | `dlopen` without ALLOW=1 | residual Err | **BLOCK** — live `set OODA_FFI_ALLOW_DLOPEN=1…` | no FN | — |
| D2 | `dlopen` `/tmp/evil.so` with ALLOW, empty ALLOWDIR | residual Err | **BLOCK** — not under system lib dirs | no FN | — |
| D3 | `dlopen` `..` outside ALLOWDIR | residual Err | **BLOCK** — realpath leave dir (qa `sec_02_ffi_traversal.oo`) | no FN | — |
| D4 | Leaf symlink after realpath | refuse / O_NOFOLLOW | **BLOCK** path-A open check; then close | no FN for leaf | — |
| D5 | Unsigned `.so` (no `.minisig`) | refuse | **FAIL-CLOSED** — live libc → `missing or invalid minisig` | no FN | — |
| D6 | Minisign PATH hijack (evil `minisign` first on PATH) | must not trust | **was CRITICAL FN** — `execlp` inherited full parent env/PATH; **OWN fix**: clearenv + abs paths + safe PATH | was FN | CRIT→mitigated |
| D7 | Minisign `LD_PRELOAD` interpose verifier | must not trust | **was CRITICAL FN** — same; **OWN fix** clearenv before exec | was FN | CRIT→mitigated |
| D8 | minisign `-P <hex fingerprint>` "FP pin" | real pin or omit | **prior broken** (wrong flag meaning); **OWN**: drop `-P` hex; residual no FP pin | doc FN | MED |
| D9 | Constructor re-enters `oo_dlopen` | refuse | **BLOCK** — `g_ffi_dlopen_depth > 0` → `nested dlopen refused` | no FN for oo_* | — |
| D10 | Constructor raw `dlopen(3)` / RCE | residual | **residual** — path-A does not sandbox signed ctor TCB | residual | HIGH |
| D11 | Replace `.so` bytes after minisig, before `dlopen` | residual TOCTOU | **residual** — verify path then `dlopen(rp_path)` | residual FN class | HIGH |
| D12 | Concurrent `oo_dlopen` races on handle table | serialize | **path-A** mutex + depth | no FN table smash | — |
| D13 | `dlsym` after concurrent `dlclose` | residual UAF | **residual** — no refcount | residual | MED |
| W1 | Write without `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` | deny | **BLOCK** — live deny | no FN | — |
| W2 | Write `..` outside writedir | deny | **BLOCK** — live deny | no FN | — |
| W3 | Write relative path | deny | **BLOCK** — requires absolute | no FN | — |
| W4 | Existing symlink leaf → outside | deny | **BLOCK** — realpath leaves dir | no FN | — |
| W5 | Swap regular→symlink between allow and open | deny | **BLOCK** — `openat(O_NOFOLLOW)` | no FN | — |
| W6 | Create new file under writedir | allow | **ALLOW** — parent realpath + create (`new ok=1`) | no FP | — |
| W7 | Hardlink outside file into writedir, then write | deny or document | **BYPASS** — live `ok=1`, outside target becomes `PWNED_HARD` | **FN** | **HIGH** |
| W8 | Parent dir rename race | residual | **residual** — comment in `writedir_open_trunc` | residual | MED |
| W9 | open-after-realpath using original `path.data` (old bug) | must use sealed open | **sealed on tip** — `writedir_open_trunc` + `fdopen`; no raw `fopen(path.data)` for write | was FN | — |

